# The environment the SUITE assumes, declared where every runner can see it.
#
# vitest runs in mode "test", so Vite loads .env, .env.test and .env.local, and never
# .env.development. VITE_APP_BASE_DOMAIN lived only in .env.local, which is gitignored, so
# subdomain.test.ts passed on a machine that had once run the dev server and failed on a fresh
# clone and on CI. `getSubdomainType` reads the value through import.meta.env, which Vite replaces
# at transform time, so the test assigning it at runtime cannot rescue an absent one.
#
# Tracked on purpose. A suite that only passes next to somebody's untracked file is the same
# class of vacuity as a timezone pin that does not apply.
VITE_APP_BASE_DOMAIN=localhost
